{'bigquery-public-data': {'census_bureau_international': ['midyear_population', 'birth_death_growth_rates', 'country_names_area', 'midyear_population_agespecific', 'midyear_population_5yr_age_sex', 'midyear_population_age_sex', 'age_specific_fertility_rates', 'mortality_life_expectancy']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  
• `midyear_population_agespecific.age` : to isolate the exact ages (< 25) we want.  
• `midyear_population_agespecific.population` : the head‑count for each single year of age (split by sex).  
• `midyear_population_agespecific.year` / `country_code` / `country_name` : filter to 2017 and aggregate by country.  
• `midyear_population.midyear_population` : total 2017 population for the same country (needed for the denominator).  
Main conditions  
• `WHERE year = 2017`  
• `AND age < 25` (for the numerator)  

Below are ten exploratory → final queries (all `LIMIT 20`) that progressively build up to the answer.

```sql
-- Description: 1) Peek at 2017 rows in the age‑specific table.
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
WHERE year = 2017
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 2) Check which ages are present for 2017.
SELECT DISTINCT age
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
WHERE year = 2017
ORDER BY age
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 3) Look at a single country’s age distribution (e.g., India).
SELECT country_name, sex, age, population
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
WHERE year = 2017
  AND country_name = 'India'
ORDER BY age
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 4) Aggregate under‑25 population by country (still split by sex).
SELECT country_name,
       sex,
       SUM(population) AS pop_u25
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
WHERE year = 2017
  AND age < 25
GROUP BY country_name, sex
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 5) Combine sexes → total under‑25 population per country.
SELECT country_name,
       SUM(population) AS pop_u25
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
WHERE year = 2017
  AND age < 25
GROUP BY country_name
ORDER BY pop_u25 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 6) Get total 2017 population from the midyear table.
SELECT country_name,
       midyear_population AS total_pop_2017
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population`
WHERE year = 2017
ORDER BY total_pop_2017 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 7) Join the two aggregates (under‑25 & total) for 2017.
SELECT u.country_name,
       u.pop_u25,
       t.midyear_population AS total_pop_2017
FROM (
  SELECT country_code, country_name, SUM(population) AS pop_u25
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
  WHERE year = 2017
    AND age < 25
  GROUP BY country_code, country_name
) AS u
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` AS t
  ON u.country_code = t.country_code
WHERE t.year = 2017
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 8) Compute the percentage of population under 25 for each country.
SELECT u.country_name,
       u.pop_u25,
       t.midyear_population AS total_pop_2017,
       100.0 * u.pop_u25 / t.midyear_population AS pct_u25
FROM (
  SELECT country_code, country_name, SUM(population) AS pop_u25
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
  WHERE year = 2017
    AND age < 25
  GROUP BY country_code, country_name
) AS u
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` AS t
  ON u.country_code = t.country_code
WHERE t.year = 2017
ORDER BY pct_u25 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 9) Show only the country with the highest % under‑25 (ties kept).
SELECT u.country_name,
       ROUND(100.0 * u.pop_u25 / t.midyear_population, 2) AS pct_u25
FROM (
  SELECT country_code, country_name, SUM(population) AS pop_u25
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
  WHERE year = 2017
    AND age < 25
  GROUP BY country_code, country_name
) AS u
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` AS t
  ON u.country_code = t.country_code
WHERE t.year = 2017
ORDER BY pct_u25 DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 10) FINAL – return only the #1 country (highest % under‑25) for 2017.
SELECT country_name,
       ROUND(pct_u25, 2) AS pct_population_under_25_2017
FROM (
  SELECT u.country_name,
         100.0 * u.pop_u25 / t.midyear_population AS pct_u25,
         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY 100.0 * u.pop_u25 / t.midyear_population DESC) AS rn
  FROM (
    SELECT country_code, country_name, SUM(population) AS pop_u25
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_agespecific`
    WHERE year = 2017
      AND age < 25
    GROUP BY country_code, country_name
  ) AS u
  JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` AS t
    ON u.country_code = t.country_code
  WHERE t.year = 2017
)
WHERE rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```
